<h1>SPHEREx: An All-Sky Spectral Survey</h1>

<center>
<table cellpadding=10>
<tr>
<td style="text-align:center" width="200"><a href="/applications/spherex"><img src="/images/icons/missions/SPHEREx_iconD.jpg" alt="" width="70" /></a>
            <div><h3 style="border:none;"><a href="/applications/spherex">SPHEREx Data Explorer</a></h3></div></td>
<td style="text-align:center" width="200"><a href="/data/SPHEREx/docs/overview_dr1.html"><img src="/images/icons/Documentation_blue.jpg" alt="" width="70" /></a>
            <div><h3 style="border:none;"><a href="/data/SPHEREx/docs/overview_dr1.html">Documentation</a></h3></div></td>
</tr>
</table>
</center>


<h3>Mission Characteristics</h3>


<table class="striped" align="center">
<tr>
    <td class="th"><b>Lifetime:</b></td>
    <td class="tc">2025 - 2027 (planned)</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
    <td class="th"><b>Wavelength:</b></td>
    <td class="tc"> 0.75-1.1 microns, R=39<br />
     1.1-1.6 microns, R=41<br />
     1.6-2.4 microns, R=41<br />
     2.4-3.8 microns, R=35<br />
     3.8-4.4 microns, R=112<br />
     4.4-5.0 microns, R=128 </td>
</tr>
<tr>
    <td class="th"><b>Area Coverage (planned):</b></td>
    <td class="tc">100% of sky</td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
    <td class="th"><b>Instruments:</b></td>
    <td class="tc">
        Wide Field Linear Variable Filter (LVF) Imaging Spectrograph
    </td>
</tr>
<tr >
    <td class="th"><b>Funding Agency:</b></td>
    <td class="tc">
        NASA
    </td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
    <td class="th"><b>Contributing Institutions:</b></td>
    <td class="tc">
        JPL, Caltech, RIT, Harvard/CFA, Arizona State, University of Arizona, Ohio State University, KASI, UC Irvine, Johns Hopkins, ASIAA
    </td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class="th"><b>Acknowledgement:</b></td>
<td class="tc">
Please include the following acknowledgement in any published material that makes use of SPHEREx data products:<br /><i>
"This publication makes use of data products from the Spectro-Photometer for the History of the Universe, Epoch of Reionization and Ices Explorer (SPHEREx), which is a joint project of the Jet Propulsion Laboratory and the California Institute of Technology, and is funded by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration."</i>
</td>
</tr>

<tr>
    <td class="th"><b>Canonical Papers:</b></td>
    <td class="tc">
        Mission: <a href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2026ApJ...999..139B/abstract" target="_blank">Bock et al (2026)</a><br />
        Pipeline: <a href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2026ApJS..285...67A/abstract" target="_blank">Akeson et al (2026)</a><br />
        Sky Simulator: <a href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2025ApJS..281...10C/abstract" target="_blank">Crill et al. (2025)</a><br />
        Instrument &amp; Calibration: <a href="https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/2026arXiv260329835K/abstract" target="_blank">Korngut et al. (2026)</a><br />
    </td>
</tr>
<tr class="even">
    <td class="th"><b>SPHEREx Releases:</b></td>
    <td class="tc">July 2025: <a href="/data/SPHEREx/docs/overview_qr.html">First Quick Release Products available at IRSA</a><br /> 
	October 2025: <a href="/data/SPHEREx/docs/overview_qr.html">First reprocessed Quick Release Products (QR2) available at IRSA</a><br >
    April 10, 2026: <a href="/data/SPHEREx/docs/psfhdrerr.html">QR2 headers updated to correct PSF extension header error (see documentation for details)</a><br />
    September 2026: <a href="/data/SPHEREx/docs/overview_qr.html">First Quick Release 3 (QR3) Products available at IRSA</a><br />
    November 2026: <a href="/data/SPHEREx/docs/overview_dr1.html">Data Release 1 (DR1) Products available at IRSA</a>
    </td>
</tr>
</table>


